# Bug: Permissions schema update not working correctly

## Description

I've discovered a bug in the permissions cog where the schema update functionality is completely broken. When updating from an old permissions configuration to the new format, no rules are being migrated.

## Steps to reproduce

1. Have an existing bot with permissions configured in the old format
2. Update to the latest version
3. Notice that all previously configured permissions are gone

## Code that demonstrates the issue

```python
from redbot.cogs.permissions.permissions import Permissions

# Example of old config format
old_config = {
    "0": {
        "owner_models": {
            "cogs": {
                "Admin": {
                    "allow": [78631113035100160],
                    "deny": [96733288462286848]
                },
                "Audio": {
                    "allow": [133049272517001216],
                    "default": "deny"
                }
            },
            "commands": {
                "cleanup bot": {
                    "allow": [78631113035100160],
                    "default": "deny"
                },
                "ping": {
                    "allow": [96733288462286848],
                    "deny": [96733288462286848],
                    "default": "allow"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

# This should convert the old format to the new format
# but returns empty dictionaries instead
new_cog_rules, new_cmd_rules = Permissions._get_updated_schema(old_config)
print(new_cog_rules)  # Returns {}
print(new_cmd_rules)  # Returns {}
```

## Expected behavior

The function should convert the old permission format to the new one, preserving all the rules that were previously set.

## Actual behavior

The function returns empty dictionaries, effectively wiping out all previously configured permissions.

## Environment

- Red Discord Bot version: 3.5.0
- Python version: 3.10
- OS: Ubuntu 22.04

Before/after of the live bot are uploaded — open `perms-panel-before-3.4.png` first, then `perms-panel-after-3.5.png`, then the REPL shot `schema-update-repl.png`. Those three are what showed me the rules vanishing; the dict in the ticket was copied from the first panel.

